0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#the-three-listeners-have-different-trust-levels","title":"The three listeners have different trust levels"},{"depth":2,"url":"#turn-on-tls","title":"Turn on TLS"},{"depth":2,"url":"#make-the-client-prove-who-it-is","title":"Make the client prove who it is"},{"depth":2,"url":"#point-clients-at-the-new-scheme","title":"Point clients at the new scheme"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-experimental_identity_header-actually-does","title":["What ",["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_identity_header"}]," actually does"]},{"depth":2,"url":"#credentials-to-an-upstream-service","title":"Credentials to an upstream service"},{"depth":2,"url":"#steps","title":"Steps"},{"depth":2,"url":"#when-it-doesnt-work","title":"When it doesn't work"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"TLS and authentication"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"Put TLS on the listeners clients reach, use mutual TLS as the access control, and understand exactly what Forge does and does not authenticate."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone about to expose Forge beyond a single trusted\nnetwork. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," encrypted listeners, client\ncertificates as the gate, and an accurate picture of what is still unguarded.\n",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," an hour, most of it spent on certificates."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["A running deployment you can restart. See ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/production-config","children":"Production configuration"}],"."]}]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Start with the honest version, because it changes what you build."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Forge has no user accounts, no password, no token check and no\nauthorization rules. Nothing in the binary decides whether a\nparticular caller is allowed to read a particular blob. The access control you\nget is ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"mutual TLS"}]," (the listener refuses connections from clients that\ncannot present a certificate signed by a CA you name) plus whatever your\nnetwork already does. Everything past the handshake is trusted equally."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"That is a coherent security model, and it is the one to build. It is not the\nmodel you would get from a system with an architect table, so it pays to be explicit\nabout it before you plan around a feature that does not exist."}],"\n",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-config/src/cas_server.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-config/src/cas_server.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-config/src/cas_server.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"TlsConfig"]}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-three-listeners-have-different-trust-levels","children":"The three listeners have different trust levels"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"A production deployment exposes three surfaces, and they do not want the