2d:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"headers"}]," are static and sent on every request. Note that, unlike most string\nfields in the config, header values are not run through ",["$","code",null,{"children":"$${VAR}"}]," expansion:\nthe value in the file is sent verbatim, so a secret placed here lives in the\nfile and the file needs to be protected accordingly. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forward_headers"}]," takes a\nlist of header names to copy from the incoming client request instead, which is\nhow a client's own credential reaches the upstream without Forge holding\none. Forwarding is incompatible with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_read_batching"}],", and a store\nthat configures both is rejected at startup."]}]
